## 2. Components & patterns

- **Chat input (Grok style):** large rounded pill/rounded-2xl glass field, auto-growing textarea, attach + model/agent selector left, round send button right (disabled state visible), `Enter` = send, `Shift+Enter` = newline, streaming indicator, stop button while generating.
- **Messages:** user message right in elev-2 bubble; assistant left, no bubble, plain readable text, markdown + code blocks with copy button.
- **Settings:** left nav (desktop) / stacked list with back arrow (mobile). Every section opens. Rows: label + description + control right. Save is automatic with a small "Gespeichert" toast, or explicit with a sticky footer – never both.
- **Menus & context menus:** frosted `.menu`, keyboard navigable (Radix/shadcn primitives preferred), destructive items red and last, with undo toast ("Entfernt · Rückgängig").
- **Lists (agents, tabs, companies):** icon/favicon/avatar 32–40px, title, muted subtitle, chevron or status dot. Grouped with small uppercase muted section labels.
- **Empty states:** icon, one sentence, one primary action. Never a blank page.
- **Skeletons** instead of spinners for content; spinner only inside buttons.
- **Toasts:** bottom center (mobile) / bottom right (desktop), glass, auto-dismiss 4s, errors stay until dismissed and say what to do.

## 3. Signed-out experience

- If the user is not authenticated, show a **landing page**, not an error or empty app: ambient glow, product name, one-line value proposition, 3 feature points max, primary button "Mit Google fortfahren", footer links Impressum · Datenschutz · Nutzungsbedingungen.
- After login, go straight into the app at the last visited route. Logout must work on desktop and mobile and return to the landing page.

## 4. Mobile (≤ 768px)

- **Minimalism:** no bottom tab bar unless asked. Main sections are swiped left/right (CSS scroll-snap or a gesture lib), with small page dots as orientation.
- Secondary navigation (company switch, account, settings) hides behind the avatar.
- Bottom sheets (glass, drag handle, snap points) instead of modals.
- Touch targets ≥ 44px, respect `env(safe-area-inset-*)`, no horizontal overflow, inputs ≥ 16px font (no iOS zoom).
- Test at 390×844 and 360×740.

## 5. Motion

- Tasteful, fast, purposeful: 120–320ms, `--ease-out`. Fade + 4–8px translate for enter; scale 0.98 for press.
- Use Framer Motion / CSS transitions; animate `opacity` and `transform` only.
- No bouncing, no infinite decorative loops, no parallax gimmicks. Max one ambient effect per screen.
- Always honor `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` → disable transforms, keep opacity.

## 6. Language & copy (Stefan's apps)

- **UI text in German**, short and direct, "du"-form: "Speichern", "Abbrechen", "Einstellungen", "Abmelden", "Mit Google fortfahren", "Neuer Chat", "Unternehmen wechseln", "Gespeichert", "Etwas ist schiefgelaufen – erneut versuchen".
- Error messages say what happened and what to do, no stack traces or HTTP codes in the main text (put them in "Details").
- No lorem ipsum, no "TODO", no English leftovers in German UIs. Keep product names as they are (Connect, Helium, Notch).
- Code, identifiers and commit messages in English.

## 7. Accessibility

- Semantic HTML first (`button`, `nav`, `main`, `dialog`), labels for every input, `aria-label` for icon-only buttons.
- Full keyboard support: Tab order, `Esc` closes overlays, focus trap in dialogs, focus returns to trigger.
- Contrast ≥ 4.5:1 for text (muted text on --bg must still pass for body copy).
- Visible focus via `--focus-ring` everywhere. Never `outline: none` without replacement.

## 8. TypeScript & React standards

- `"strict": true`, no `any` (use `unknown` + narrowing), no `@ts-ignore` without a comment explaining why.
- Small components (< ~150 lines); extract hooks (`useX`) for logic; one component per file for shared UI.
- Props typed with explicit interfaces; discriminated unions for states (`{status:'loading'} | {status:'error', error} | {status:'ok', data}`).
- Server/client boundaries respected (Next.js: `"use client"` only where needed). Data fetching via existing client/query layer (e.g. TanStack Query, server actions) – don't add a new one.
- Validate external input (zod). Handle errors explicitly; no silent `catch {}`.
- No new dependency without a reason stated in the reply; prefer what's already installed (shadcn/ui, Radix, Tailwind, lucide, framer-motion).
- Delete dead code you replace. No commented-out blocks.

## 9. Definition of Done

Before saying "fertig", confirm:
- [ ] Typecheck, lint, tests green (or explain what couldn't run).
- [ ] Checked desktop + mobile, dark (+ light if toggle exists), keyboard.
- [ ] Loading / empty / error states present.
- [ ] All labels German, no placeholders, no dead buttons.
- [ ] No invented APIs; no secrets committed; backup made before risky changes.
- [ ] Short summary: what changed, what was verified, what is still open.
